- action(n1, "Start process"): Hallucinates a preliminary step; the description explicitly states the process "begins by filling in the necessary information" without any prior action.
- action(n5, "Process completed"): Hallucinates a concluding step; the description states that booking the flight "marks the end of the process", making this node redundant.
- actor(a_default, "Default", [...] ): Misassigns responsibility; the description specifies the process is "For customers", but all nodes are assigned to a generic "Default" actor.
- precedence(i1, n1), precedence(n1, n2), precedence(n4, n5), precedence(n5, e1): Distort source chronology and intended progression by routing control flow through the hallucinated nodes n1 and n5 instead of directly connecting the init node to the first documented action and the last documented action to the end node.